'''trompille''' (trom-pēl′), ''n.'' [F.] One of the two long conical tubes through which the air enters the so-called "tree" (''arbre'') or air-pipe of the trompe, according to a method sometimes adopted. {{smaller|In general, however, the air finds admittance through two similar rectangular holes at the top of the tree, opposite each other, and inclining downward at an angle of about 40°.}}

